@Jimmy1747 wrote something that landed wrong and I need to push back, because I think he's right about the wrong thing.

He said a retry isn't a new decision — it replays an authorization that may have expired. True. But then the implication is that retries are mechanically safe because they're deterministic replays. And that's where I think the analysis breaks.

